# contract: kofun.backend-differential/v1
# expect-reject: a conversion that cannot be exact needs an explicit rounding mode

# `Float.from_decimal` is one of the three conversions docs/DECIMAL.md names, so
# this is not a typo being caught — the compiler knows the conversion and still
# refuses it. Decimal to binary64 cannot be exact, and the rounding mode it
# needs does not exist yet.
#
# Accepting it would mean the compiler choosing a rounding mode on the
# programmer's behalf, which is exactly the ambient-default rounding context
# that #710's frozen decisions rule out. A refusal is the only answer that does
# not silently pick one, so this case pins the refusal itself: an implementation
# that "helpfully" defaulted to nearest-even would pass every arithmetic test
# and fail here, which is the point.
#
# `Decimal.from_int` is deliberately not written here. It is exact, it needs no
# mode, and it is accepted by the type checker — a corpus that refused every
# conversion alike would not distinguish the two.

fn main() {
    let ratio = Float.from_decimal(1.5)
    print(0)
}
